  <title id="bdl02entropymcmc-title">Entropy-MCMC sampling dynamics on an energy landscape</title>
  <desc id="bdl02entropymcmc-desc">Contour lines show an energy landscape with a sharp, narrow minimum at the bottom right and a wide, flat basin at the top right. On the left, the parameter theta has an original gradient direction, gradient of f, pointing to the right; the coupling term one over eta times theta minus theta a points up toward the auxiliary variable theta a; their sum, the flatness-aware gradient direction, gradient of U, points up and to the right, away from the sharp minimum. A dashed path leads to a second position of theta, where the arrows again point upward toward the flat region and the nearby theta a.</desc>
